{{!
  Klabis customization: emits a Java record instead of the default generator's mutable class.

  Rationale: hand-written Klabis response/request DTOs are records (see backend-patterns skill —
  MemberDetailsResponse, AddressResponse, GuardianDTO, ...). MapStruct maps into these records by
  calling the canonical constructor with named-argument resolution against record components, and
  @RecordBuilder (io.soabase.recordbuilder) needs a genuine record to generate a builder.
  The stock JavaSpring pojo.mustache only emits classes with getters/setters, so this file replaces
  it wholesale rather than patching it.

  additionalModelTypeAnnotations (configOptions) carries @RecordBuilder / @JsonInclude /
  @HandleAuthorizationDenied uniformly - see build.gradle.kts. They are harmless no-ops on models
  that don't need them.
}}
/**
 * {{description}}{{^description}}{{classname}}{{/description}}
 */
{{>additionalModelTypeAnnotations}}
{{>generatedAnnotation}}
public record {{classname}}(
    {{! Field-level security: x-klabis-* extensions on the spec property map 1:1 onto the
        annotations documented in the klabis-api-spec skill. They render as parameter annotations,
        same position as on the hand-written records (see backend-patterns: @OwnerId MemberId id).

        Bean Validation constraints (@Email, @Size, @Pattern, ...) come from the stock
        JavaSpring beanValidation partial so request-side schemas (e.g. GuardianDTO, shared between
        RegisterMemberRequest and MemberDetailsResponse) keep the same runtime validation the
        hand-written DTOs had.

        @NotBlank and @Past are the exceptions: OpenAPI has no keyword for either ("not blank",
        "strictly in the past"), so they come from x-klabis-not-blank / x-klabis-past rather than
        the partial. A field that is both `required` and not-blank therefore carries a redundant
        @NotNull from the partial as well; that is harmless, and suppressing it would mean forking
        the stock beanValidation template too.

        x-klabis-patch-field wraps the component in JsonNullable<T>, giving a PATCH body the
        absent/null/value tri-state. It is a Klabis extension rather than the generator's own
        openApiNullable option because that option keys off `nullable`, which openapi-generator
        ignores in OpenAPI 3.1 mode — verified against both `nullable: true` and the 3.1 spelling
        `type: [x, "null"]`; neither produced a JsonNullable. The type is fully qualified so
        model.mustache needs no extra import. }}
    {{#vars}}{{^-first}},
    {{/-first}}{{#vendorExtensions.x-klabis-owner-id}}@com.klabis.common.security.fieldsecurity.OwnerId {{/vendorExtensions.x-klabis-owner-id}}{{#vendorExtensions.x-klabis-owner-visible}}@com.klabis.common.security.fieldsecurity.OwnerVisible {{/vendorExtensions.x-klabis-owner-visible}}{{#vendorExtensions.x-klabis-authority}}@com.klabis.common.users.HasAuthority(com.klabis.common.users.Authority.{{.}}) {{/vendorExtensions.x-klabis-authority}}{{#vendorExtensions.x-klabis-halforms-access}}@com.klabis.common.ui.HalForms(access = com.klabis.common.ui.HalForms.Access.{{.}}) {{/vendorExtensions.x-klabis-halforms-access}}{{#vendorExtensions.x-klabis-not-blank}}@jakarta.validation.constraints.NotBlank {{/vendorExtensions.x-klabis-not-blank}}{{#vendorExtensions.x-klabis-past}}@jakarta.validation.constraints.Past {{/vendorExtensions.x-klabis-past}}{{#useBeanValidation}}{{>beanValidation}}{{/useBeanValidation}}{{#vendorExtensions.x-klabis-patch-field}}org.openapitools.jackson.nullable.JsonNullable<{{{datatypeWithEnum}}}> {{name}}{{/vendorExtensions.x-klabis-patch-field}}{{^vendorExtensions.x-klabis-patch-field}}{{{datatypeWithEnum}}} {{name}}{{/vendorExtensions.x-klabis-patch-field}}{{/vars}}
) {
